
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://www.teachphilosophy101.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">TeachPhilosophy101</a>, a free and helpful collection of resources and ideas for teaching philosophy, has recently been updated.</p>



<span id="more-26106"></span>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full is-resized"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="883" height="955" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Henri-Florence-Struttura.png" alt="" class="wp-image-26107" style="aspect-ratio:0.9246110748956112;width:485px;height:auto" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Henri-Florence-Struttura.png 883w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Henri-Florence-Struttura-277x300.png 277w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Henri-Florence-Struttura-768x831.png 768w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Henri-Florence-Struttura-231x250.png 231w" sizes="(max-width: 883px) 100vw, 883px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">&#8220;Struttúra&#8221; by Florence Henri</figcaption></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Its materials cover course planning, how to use class time, student assessment, challenges, and much more. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TeachPhilosophy101  was created by <a href="https://johnimmerwahr.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">John Immerwahr</a> (Villanova) and <a href="https://dailynous.com/free-resources-for-philosophy-teachers/">previously revamped</a> by <a href="https://app.oxford.emory.edu/WebApps/Directory/index.cfm/view/9252" data-type="link" data-id="https://app.oxford.emory.edu/WebApps/Directory/index.cfm/view/9252" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Erin Tarver</a> (Emory). Recently <a href="https://www.arapahoe.edu/employees/david-sackris-phd" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">David Sackris</a> (Arapahoe Community College) took over as editor of the site, making further changes and adding additional resources. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Some of those new resources come by way of an arrangement with the <a href="https://www.pdcnet.org/wp/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Philosophy Documentation Center</a> and the journal, <em><a href="https://www.pdcnet.org/teachphil" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Teaching Philosophy</a></em>, to provide free access to any articles in the journal that are linked to on the TeachPhilosophy101 site.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It&#8217;s very much <a href="https://www.teachphilosophy101.org/">worth checking out</a>.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">And if you&#8217;d like to contribute materials or ideas for TeachPhilosophy101 , <a href="mailto:d26988123@gmail.com">email Professor Sackris</a>.</p>
